mod:variadic_tail_whole;
// 2026-11-15 (landing 177d2b7, row 5: DEF-670). A VARIADIC TAIL HANDED WHOLE IS A VIEW OF THIS FRAME'S CALL. A `..*T[]:vs` tail is storage the
// call builds for this frame (DEF-519), but `got_carries_frame_view` skipped every PASS ref as "a parameter's value carried: older than this frame",
// so the tail handed whole to a callee that stores it through a parameter (`setsv(w2, vs)`) went unrefused, and the caller read the dead frame after
// the call. `escape_whole_tail` takes a PASS ref as the tail itself when its place is the tail's name and it was read at the tail's own type or not
// at all; an element read out of the tail (`vs[0i64]`) is the caller's value, as before. `collect_base_refs`'s hop onto a parameter gives the tail's
// own address its PASS ref too (`int32[]->:pv = @vs; setsv(w2, <-pv)`, DEF-670's address road), which the tail is no `DeclParamDecl` to give.
// One cell a face, its names suffixed with the cell's. Each face is accepted by main (78f9b3a) and reads the dead frame there: 83 at -O0 and under
// the detector on roads 0 to 2, 255 at -O2 (`a_lst` and `a_lstl` read the old value, 67, at -O2). Each right control is in `variadic_tail_whole_ok.npk`.
// W1's 17 (Ailp-team_141's cells): `a1_cp` to `a10_gen`, the tail handed whole through a copy, a field, a call, a loop, a branch, a cast, an
// identity call, a method, a ternary and a generic; `vt1`, `vt1c`, `vt1n`, `vt1t`, `vt2`, `vt5`, `vt6`, the name road. a145's five: `a_lst`, `a_lstl`,
// `a_mksv`, `a_sfld`, `a_var2`. The address road's four (a145's): `a_adr`, `a_adri`, `a_adrv`, `a_adrs`; main refuses their frame twin `a_adrl`.
// This seat's nine, the tail read at an Optional type (`int32[]?:o = vs;`, through `??`, `??!`, an address and an Optional field): `vto1` to `vto9`;
// `vto8` and `vto9` take the address road (`int32[]->:pv = @vs; int32[]?:o = <-pv;`).
// THE ROW'S REFUSED CONTROLS: the seven `vt*_ok` each store the dead tail through a parameter, which DEF-519's ruling refuses, as main refuses
// `vt1d_ok` (management's ruling of 2026-11-15, row 5: "The `vt*_ok` controls aren't prices."). The four at parity, `a_ret2_ok`, `a_cpy_ok`,
// `a_cpyx_ok`, `a_cpyl_ok`, run 67 on main: the row reads a tail handed whole as a slice of a frame array, and main refuses the same callees handed
// such a slice (`a_retf_ok`, `a_cpyf_ok`).
error:E5;
struct:SV_a_adr = { int32[]:s; };
